		"nodes": {
			"19": {
				"attributes": {
					"alignment": {
						"type": "integer",
						"value": 0
					},
					"fill": {
						"type": "bool",
						"value": true
					},
					"font-size": {
						"type": "float",
						"value": 19
					},
					"text": {
						"type": "string",
						"value": "NEGATE\nThe Negate node negates the incoming value. Basically meaning that any negative input becomes positive and any positive input becomes negative. This also works on shapes (see last example).\n\nExample A: -2 becomes 2.\nExample B:  5 becomes -5.\n\nThe following patch contains all the basic rounding functions in Wire.\nUse the slider to adjust the value that is to be rounded.\nThe height of the red rectangle is directly modulated by the value slider.\nThe height of the brown rectangle is modulated by the negated value.\n\nPatch Explained -\n\n• The slider provides a value between -5 and 5 to the rounding nodes. The Join node combines their values in an array so we can adres each instance of the rectangle in the Transform node."
					}
				},
				"bounds": {
					"height": 337,
					"width": 811,
					"x": 280.5999755859375,
					"y": -53
				},
				"class": {
					"id": "77697265-3C1D-467D-A722-0FC566538374",
					"version": 1
				},
				"clock": "video",
				"color": "ffd0c117",
